# Tracker Bug Search: owner contract v1

Next source-only cancellation delta adds `runtime_custody.disposition =
never_started_removed` to the existing100 never-submitted endpoint. It requires
a closed positive Base proof: contract_version1, original operation/resource/
context/generation/container IDs, registration/request SHA256, state observed
and observation never_started_removed. Context must equal the outer custody;
the canonical proof digest is checked before the atomic retained receipt and
capacity release. This is distinct from NamespaceExited: it proves an original
registered container was fenced against start and removed without force, not
that a native run existed or completed. Exact configured Fleet attestation is
still mandatory, including protective replay after owner revocation. Tracker101
unknown submissions and actual runtime terminal remain NamespaceExited-only.
No migration, new endpoint or historical receipt rewrite is needed. PG/HTTP and
SDK259 qualification of this delta are UNRUN;975161 remains an unchanged export.

`BugSourceIdentity.repository_id` — optional canonical repository UUID с
default None и omission при сериализации None. Новые findings для snapshot с
`targets[].source` обязаны передать UUID репозитория из этого исходного record;
`checked_version` равен commit SHA именно этого target, в том числе для QA.
Delivery ref не подменяет checked commit. Поэтому одинаковые rule/key/report/SHA
из разных репозиториев дают разные source hashes и разные canonical Bugs.
Проверка действует и перед новой регистрацией, и для terminal result whitelist.
Старые source-less snapshot/report hashes и original-key receipts не переписываются;
UUID из opaque refs/текста/URL не выводится. Новый delta пока source-only, без rollout.

Source candidate, 18 October 2026. No rollout or live project search is enabled.
The source candidate implements scoped capability/grant reads, accepted policy
CAS, manual search reservation/admission and atomic finding registration.
Periodic due/cancel, intake assignment and verification
business transitions remain subsequent work. The next source candidate also
contains protective terminal acceptance and late typed result delivery; it is not
part of the first immutable 30-file export and requires its own qualification. Workflow preparation is attested
by the exact Fleet coordinator after producer readback; this is not a caller
boolean or a generic human permission. No periodic scheduler is added.

## Identity and authority

`TASKTRACKER_BUG_SEARCH__FLEET_SUBJECT` identifies the Fleet coordinator. Its own
Central PAT has only `task-tracker:read`/`task-tracker:write`. The separate
`TASKTRACKER_BUG_SEARCH__WORKFLOW_READER_SUBJECT` has exactly
`task-tracker:read` on its own PAT. Workflow and CI service PATs are never forwarded
to Tracker. The agent receives neither credential. Runtime authority is Workflow's
execution/run token, checked against the retained Tracker delegation.

Configuration is opt-in and absent by default. Both subjects must differ from
each other and existing PM/orchestrator/verifier/scheduler subjects. New subjects
are refused by generic human API mapping and restricted to project Bug routes
by the strict Central route layer. A configured flag does not grant old PM
assignment/reservation or generic issue creation authority.

The opaque `TASKTRACKER_SDLC__INSTANCE_ID` remains the existing locator.
`TT_NAMESPACE__INSTANCE_ID` provides an explicit, nonnil canonical Tracker resource
instance UUID. Grant binding returns both `tracker_instance_id` and
`tracker_instance_uuid`; a project Namespace projection must agree with the UUID.
No alias-to-UUID cast or guessed cross-product mapping is used.

Active users are resolved by exact central subject. Capability reads require a
verified human session and explicit project ownership/membership. The management
authority observation compares actual `projects.owner_id`, independently of the
legacy central-mode project bypass. Archived/missing Namespace projections block
writes. Existing member roles are not silently promoted to management authority.

## HTTP surface

All paths below begin `/api/v1/projects/{project_id}/sdlc`; responses use
`Cache-Control: no-store` and generated OpenAPI DTOs.

| Method and suffix | Authority / result |
| --- | --- |
| PUT `/bug-search/policy` | Exact Fleet write principal attests a freshly authorized human command; `owner_subject` must be the active actual project owner. CAS compares `expected_revision` with Tracker head (0 initially); `desired_revision` must be higher and may skip unapplied Fleet drafts. |
| GET `/bug-search/policy` | Exact Fleet read principal, current retained-owner/project/Namespace read ACL; current accepted head only. |
| GET `/bug-search/operations/{idempotency_key}` | Exact original Fleet actor/project/key and fresh retained-owner ACL. Immutable `{kind:policy|reserve|admit|register,result:<typed acceptance>}`; recovers old policy receipt after newer revisions. |
| POST `/bug-search/executions` | Exact Fleet write attestation/current project owner, exact accepted policy revision/owner/targets/scope and full typed immutable snapshot/hash. Tracker mints execution/fence/grant and holds shared capacity. Only manual search is currently supported; disabled periodic policy still allows manual search. |
| POST `/bug-search/executions/{execution_id}/admit` | Exact Fleet write principal, active reserved binding/fence/custody and canonical full inner prepared Workflow receipt. Exact binding, snapshot/profession/mode/version and null runtime pins are checked. |
| POST `/bug-search/executions/{execution_id}/terminal` | Next candidate: exact retained Fleet machine/fence plus independently observed actual runtime terminal identity. Works after owner revocation/Namespace archive, only records evidence/releases custody. Optional exact Workflow result does not replace actual runtime proof. |
| GET `/bug-search/capabilities` | Current human/project authority. `can_manage_policy` is the project-owner authority observation; `can_admit`, `can_register`, `can_set_own_intake` remain false until producer paths are implemented. |
| GET `/bug-search/executions/{execution_id}/grant` | Configured Workflow reader or exact Fleet coordinator with read scope, and exact active owner/project. Returns immutable binding, expiry, revocation, admission state, `authorization_valid`, `dispatch_allowed`, bounded reasons. Reserved permits preparation only; no dispatch. |
| POST `/bugs/register-or-link` | Configured Fleet identity with write scope plus exact retained admitted, unexpired, nonrevoked execution/fence and current owner/project write authority. |
| GET `/bugs/registration-operations/{idempotency_key}` | Original Fleet actor/key/project with current read scope and owner/project/Namespace ACL. Returns the original receipt. |

The execution binding contains contract version, both Tracker instance identities,
project UUID, owner subject, execution UUID, dedicated agent UUID, purpose
`search|verification`, snapshot SHA-256, policy revision, fence, Fleet machine
subject and grant UUID. Verification additionally requires Bug UUID and expected
delivery reference; search has no fake task/root-task IDs. Snapshot and binding
identity are immutable. Grant expiry/revocation never releases capacity.

`ApplyBugSearchPolicy` is `{idempotency_key,owner_subject,expected_revision,
desired_revision,policy}`. Policy mirrors Fleet exactly: enabled, mode, targets
(repository_ref/branch_ref/target_ref), scope, excluded_paths, interval_minutes.
`BugSearchPolicyState` contains contract_version, tracker_instance_id, project_id,
owner_subject, revision, policy, policy_sha256, operation_id, accepted_at and
next_due_at (null until periodic owner-queue support is implemented).

`ReserveBugSearch` is `{idempotency_key,owner_subject,snapshot,snapshot_sha256,
expected_policy_revision,agent_id}`. Snapshot is the exact Fleet immutable JSON,
including null fields. Branch resolution and profession/profile/config pins are
Fleet producer attestations; Tracker checks the accepted catalog references,
structure/hash and current owner. It does not invent a repository catalog API.
The next source candidate uses a 35-minute lease (30-minute run bound plus
5-minute transport/control grace); the first immutable QA export used 15 minutes.
Dispatch must verify remaining authority covers the run bound. Expiry never frees
custody. Both Namespace list and binding projections include held search custody,
including expired/unknown executions.

`AdmitBugSearch` is `{idempotency_key,expected_fence,workflow_receipt,
workflow_receipt_sha256}`. `workflow_receipt` is the exact inner `result` from
Workflow `/internal/bug-search/v1/executions/{execution_id}`, excluding its
`{ok,result}` transport envelope. Its canonical hash includes
`target_observations:null`; prepared receipt has no session/run/Hermes binding.
No producer credential is forwarded. The original command receipt is historical
acceptance; dispatch/recovery must freshly GET the execution grant.

`RegisterBugFinding` contains original key, execution/finding UUIDs, expected
fence, typed `source_identity` and bounded report. Source identity is exactly
`{schema_version:1,producer,rule_key,stable_defect_key}`. Report contains title,
basis, expected, actual, reproducer, checked version and evidence refs. It cannot
select owner, assignee, issue type, workflow transition or destination project.
Fleet maps its explicit typed source into this DTO; legacy opaque identities
must not be guessed into producer/rule authority.

## Atomic registration and retained history

Additive migration 000096 creates retained project-only execution bindings,
source identity records, occurrences, original registration receipts and a small
project/execution outbox. It does not alter applied migration history. Additive 000097 adds immutable
policy revisions, the accepted head and a common actor/key control journal;
existing registration receipts are backfilled without loss. Reusing a key for
another operation kind conflicts.

Actor/key advisory lock precedes fresh user/project/binding authorization. The
source lock is scoped by project and canonical source identity. One transaction
reuses `issue_creation_receipts` and `allocate_project_issue_number`, inserts the
Bug with existing default open status and initial status history, and writes
source, occurrence, operation receipt and outbox event. The reporter is the
authenticated execution owner. Project-required custom fields that cannot be
populated by this contract block creation; no required-field bypass is used.
Issue-key conflicts from legacy writes have a bounded allocator retry.

Two executions with the same source create one Bug and separate occurrences.
The semantic basis hash includes basis/expected/actual/reproducer, excluding
checked-version/evidence/title. Same source with different basis returns 409
`source_identity_basis_conflict` for explicit review. An existing closed Bug
returns `needs_reopen` and `workflow_reopen_required`; it never silently loses
the regression or performs an illegal transition. A deleted canonical Bug
returns `suppressed` with its original identity, not a replacement Bug.
Changed body under the same key conflicts; original acceptance survives restart.

Readback and retries reauthorize before returning retained acceptance. Expiry or
revocation blocks new effects but does not hide an original accepted receipt;
changed bodies still conflict after expiry. No retry
restarts discovery. Source/occurrence/receipt rows are append-only and preserve
issue references; a business rollback cannot discard this history.

The shared existing `sdlc_reservation_capacity` lock serializes future search
capacity with PM/Analysis. Reciprocal SQL guards block the same agent in feature
work and search. Task locks precede that singleton on existing feature paths.
Unknown/expired search custody remains held until qualified terminal evidence;
this schema is not a claim that admission or stop reconciliation already works.

## Validation status

Source tests cover canonical shared UTF-8 vectors, closed/bounded DTOs, exact
static identity and old-route negative authorization; synthetic PostgreSQL tests
cover concurrent deduplication, durable replay, basis collision, regression,
injected transaction rollback, grant expiry and revoked owner. Additional source tests cover concurrent policy
CAS, simultaneous reservations, exact prepared Workflow binding, cross-kind key
conflict and original receipt recovery after head changes/lease expiry. Existing real
HTTP acceptance adds capability/policy/manual-reserve/admit/grant/register/replay and rejects new services
on old PM/reservation/generic issue routes. These tests are written; execution
qualification is pending the coordinated Base ComposeHelper gate.

PG test opt-in: `TT_TEST_DATABASE_URL` and
`TT_BUG_SEARCH_DISPOSABLE_DB=1` before any connection. The external Base helper
owns the full disposable DB and failure-safe teardown; retained rows are not
deleted to clean a shared/runtime database. No deployment/autosearch is performed.

## Protective terminal candidate (after first frozen export)

`AcceptBugSearchTerminal` is `{idempotency_key,expected_fence,workflow_receipt,
workflow_receipt_sha256,runtime_observation}`. The two Workflow fields are both
null or both present; the full inner receipt is bounded to 262 KiB. The runtime
observation is `{contract_version:1,execution_id,agent_id,session_id,session_run_id,
hermes_run_ref,terminal_status,observed_at}` with exact nonnil IDs and status
`succeeded|failed|stopped|cancelled|interrupted`. The exact Fleet producer must
construct it from its actual Hermes/session-run journal readback. A Workflow
completed phase or caller boolean is not runtime terminal proof. Observed time
must follow execution creation and cannot be in the future.

Confirmed runtime termination releases custody even while Workflow is unavailable,
owner inactive or Namespace archived. Without Workflow evidence the receipt has
`result_available=false`; no new finding can use that terminal execution.
A later independently read exact Workflow completed receipt may append its typed
result, without changing the immutable first terminal proof. Runtime tuple/status
must remain identical. Whole typed result is at most 64 KiB and 100 findings;
occurrence and source identities are unique and checked versions belong to the
immutable commit/deployment snapshot. The source hash is canonical typed identity.

Migration 000098 adds append-only result evidence. Lifecycle exceptions apply only
to the protective terminal command and a first terminal-receipt/custody-release
update with all other execution fields unchanged. They do not permit policy,
admission, new issue creation or business transitions while archived. Capacity
lock precedes execution locks on reserve/admit/terminal. The terminal receipt and
result are committed with the original command key atomically; a journal failure
rolls back release. The exact original Fleet reader can recover terminal acceptance
after owner revocation, while ordinary acceptance readbacks retain current ACL.

After a terminal result, automatic registration requires exact retained finding ID,
typed source and full report equality. New issue effects still require the active
actual owner and writable Namespace. Expiry, stopping or zero findings do not
prove a Bug fixed; explicit verification/business transitions remain unavailable.
Prepared Workflow receipts still have a 64 KiB limit. The test candidate covers
lost/late producer readback, post-terminal whitelist, archive/revocation, rollback
and both Namespace drained projections; these checks have not yet run.

QA delivery uses the retained producer `result_qualification=qa_same_version`
and independently derives the same outcome from exact confirmed before/after
Forge observations: canonical project/target, expected commit/delivery, generation,
manifest, artifact and serving identity must match. A changed/unavailable or
`qa_unconfirmed` result remains retained for review and cannot create/link a Bug.
A declared qualification string cannot substitute for those observations. QA
findings cannot be delivered early under a still-active lease to bypass this gate.
Stable partial coverage can contain valid individual findings. Source-only
registration is pinned to snapshot commit SHA; late delivery additionally requires
retained `source_pinned` evidence. Source fixtures reflect their immutable commits.

## Отмена до запуска: следующий source candidate 000100

`POST /api/v1/projects/{project_id}/sdlc/bug-search/executions/{execution_id}/cancel`
принимает только exact configured Fleet producer PAT и исходную execution/fence
привязку. Это protective операция: отзыв owner, архив Namespace или expiry не
мешают закрыть доказанно не запущенное исполнение, но не разрешают новые эффекты.
Запуск и обработка live-проектов этим endpoint не включаются.

Закрытый DTO:

```text
{
  idempotency_key, expected_fence,
  not_started_observation: {
    contract_version: 1, execution_id, agent_id, snapshot_sha256,
    journal_ref, disposition: "never_submitted", observed_at,
    runtime_custody: {
      contract_version: 1,
      disposition: "never_provisioned" | "namespace_exited",
      context_id: UUID | null,
      stop_proof: JSON | null,
      stop_proof_sha256: SHA256 | null
    }
  }
}
```

`never_submitted` означает сохранённое producer-наблюдение после атомарного
Fleet cancellation fence, исключающего будущий native submit. Отсутствие строки
или ответ HTTP об ошибке сами по себе это не доказывают. Любой submitted/unknown
dispatch требует original readback; его нельзя отменить этим путём.

`never_provisioned` требует три null-поля custody и положительный durable initial
creation/cancellation witness в Fleet journal. Если execution context/container
уже создавался, нужен `namespace_exited`: actual context UUID и исходный Base
stop receipt не более 8 KiB, exact canonical SHA256, `state=observed`,
`observation=namespace_exited`, matching agent resource UUID, valid container,
generation и snapshot identities. Stop ACK, закрытый API socket и истёкший TTL
не заменяют actual namespace exit. Связь context↔Base generation аттестует Fleet
из своего исходного журнала; Tracker не строит второй инфраструктурный verifier.

Ответ — `BugSearchCancellationReceipt` с `contract_version:1`,
`kind:cancelled_before_start`, operation/project/execution/fence,
`not_started_observation`, `custody_released:true`, `accepted_at`.
В нём нет вымышленных session/run/Hermes IDs и нет `runtime_observation`.
Общий operation readback использует `{kind:"cancel",result:<receipt>}`.
Первое принятие возвращает 201, replay — 200; ответы `Cache-Control:no-store`.

Для хранения используется существующий immutable `terminal_receipt` как union
двух execution-end receipts. Предыдущий runtime terminal и cancellation
несовместимы: попытка заменить один другим возвращает conflict.
Уже принятые findings или technical result того же execution также противоречат
`never_submitted`: cancellation отклоняется, custody остаётся held. Exclusive
execution lock сериализует эту проверку с concurrent registration/result commit.
Namespace
protective update exception уже разрешает единственную запись end receipt вместе
с `capacity_held=false`; binding/admission/policy/issue при этом не меняются.
Migration100 только добавляет command kind `cancel`, сохраняя `intake`, и узкую
protective INSERT exception для command journal. Миграции096–098 не переписаны.

Actor/key, project, capacity singleton и execution locks используются в прежнем
порядке. Exact original-body replay происходит после fresh machine/retained
binding проверки, до текущего state/TTL. Принятие receipt и освобождение capacity
атомарны; ошибка журнала откатывает оба. Иное тело под тем же ключом конфликтует.
После cancellation `authorization_valid=false` и `dispatch_allowed=false`;
original admission receipt, полученный replay, не восстанавливает разрешение.

Текущий running QA snapshot098 не содержит этот candidate. Domain/PG/HTTP tests
добавлены в source; qualified cancel и producer Fleet fence/runtime proof ещё
требуют отдельного следующего gate. Ни один caller boolean не заменяет этот
обязательный owner contract.

## Unknown native acceptance без bound run: source candidate 000101

Отмена100 не называет неизвестный результат native POST «не запускалось».
Отдельный protective endpoint:
`POST /api/v1/projects/{project_id}/sdlc/bug-search/executions/{execution_id}/abort-unbound`.

```text
{
  idempotency_key, expected_fence,
  unbound_observation: {
    contract_version: 1, execution_id, agent_id, snapshot_sha256,
    journal_ref, observed_at,
    native_submission: {
      operation_key, body_sha256, submitted_at,
      acceptance: "unknown", actual_run_ref: null
    },
    workflow_handoff: {
      disposition: "bind_and_handoff_never_submitted",
      bind_journal_ref, handoff_journal_ref, observed_at
    },
    runtime_custody: {
      contract_version: 1, disposition: "namespace_exited",
      context_id: UUID, stop_proof: original Base JSON,
      stop_proof_sha256: SHA256
    }
  }
}
```

Native operation key — исходный внешний namespace/key, отдельный от abort key;
hash — исходного immutable native request body. Required `actual_run_ref:null`
отвергает missing/string/number/boolean на десериализации. Submission timestamp
не позже наблюдения с допуском 5 секунд; наблюдение не из будущего относительно
Tracker clock с тем же допуском. Journal refs bounded 512 bytes без control chars;
original Base proof bounded 8 KiB с проверенным canonical SHA256 и закрытым DTO.

Fleet сначала сохраняет learned ACK/run ID, только потом пытается Workflow bind
и credential handoff. Для101 нужны оба положительных durable fence: bind никогда
не отправлялся И execution HMAC никогда не передавался. Любой bind/handoff attempt
либо известный run требует ordinary terminal path с реальными IDs. Отсутствие строки,
stop ACK, timeout и TTL не доказывают exit. `never_provisioned` запрещён: actual
context и original namespace exit обязательны.

Tracker требует admitted execution с retained Workflow prepared receipt и null
session/run/Hermes/result полями. Exact original Fleet identity/binding/fence
проверяются свежими, owner revocation/Namespace archive/expiry не блокируют
protective release. Occurrences/results и иной end receipt конфликтуют с101.
Capacity→exclusive execution lock исключает гонку с их принятием. Evidence,
release и command journal атомарны; original key/body replay/readback сохраняется.

Inner receipt `BugUnboundCancellationReceipt.kind="cancelled_without_bound_run"`,
`custody_released:true`, с исходным observation; operation envelope
`{kind:"abort_unbound",result:<receipt>}`. Native acceptance в истории unknown,
без runtime success, fake IDs, result qualification и Bug transition. 201 — first
acceptance,200 — replay, no-store. Additive101 расширяет command kind/protective
exception, сохраняя100/099; существующий end-receipt storage не заменяется.
DTO/PG/real HTTP tests написаны, но101 ещё не compile/qualification-qualified.

## Periodic due source candidate 000102

Используются существующие policy heads (`next_due_at`), immutable reservation
outbox и original command receipts. Новых scheduler/service/queue таблиц нет.

Exact configured Fleet read+write PAT читает
`GET /api/v1/sdlc/bug-search/due?limit=1`; другой limit отклоняется. Ответ:
`{contract_version:1,observed_at,due:null|{project_id,owner_subject,policy,
expected_due_at,due_key},blocked_reasons:[]}`. `policy` — текущая applied policy
с текущим head next_due_at. GET не резервирует и не меняет срок. При held custody
(включая unknown/expired) возвращается due:null, blocked_reasons:["capacity_busy"].
Это ожидание ресурса, не failed search и не повод для alert.

Index-driven текущие heads сортируются по (next_due_at,project_id), response
bounded1. Retained history не перебирается; inactive owner, сменившийся actual
project owner, missing/archived/wrong-instance Namespace не предлагаются. Fresh
manage проверяется повторно. Canonical opaque due_key включает ProjectRef,
точную head revision и PostgreSQL timestamp в epoch microseconds; HTTP timestamps
UTC. Consumer копирует ключ/at, не строит authority из URL или локального clock.

Reserve body100 дополняется optional `expected_due:{at,key}`. Manual требует
None/отсутствие; Periodic — exact enabled policy revision, due at/key и наступивший
DB-срок. Snapshot всё так же immutable, включая trigger=periodic. Existing shared
capacity lock атомарно исключает вторую reservation. Original due сохраняется
в `bug.search_reserved.payload.expected_due`, immutable и индексированном по
execution UUID/topic. Reserve не потребляет срок. При успешном periodic admit
next_due_at атомарно становится DBnow+policy.interval_minutes (минимум60минут).
Unknown/readback не создаёт новый occurrence и не освобождает custody.

Enabled edit сохраняет due timestamp, но revision в due_key меняется: старый
queued reserve отзывается, capacity остаётся held до100/101/actual terminal proof.
Disable очищает head next_due_at и отзывает только ещё reserved periodic grants;
already admitted run сохраняет исходный snapshot при fresh owner/project/runtime
fence. Initial enable назначает первый due DBnow+interval; immediate запуск — manual.
Original receipts после новой head revision не переписываются.

Blocked target/catalog/configuration/runtime можно отложить через
`POST /api/v1/projects/{project_id}/sdlc/bug-search/defer-due`:
`{idempotency_key,owner_subject,expected_policy_revision,expected_due:{at,key},reason}`,
reason — capacity_busy|target_unavailable|catalog_unavailable|configuration_pending|
runtime_unavailable. Fresh owner/Namespace и exact occurrence обязательны; held
reservation этого occurrence требует reconcile и не откладывается. Owner фиксирует
DBnow+5минут, без caller timestamp/backoff knobs. Таким образом один неисправный
проект не блокирует другие due heads. Receipt `BugSearchDueDeferral` содержит
contract_version,operation_id,tracker_instance_id,project_id,owner_subject,
policy_revision,previous_due,next_due_at,reason,accepted_at; command envelope
`{kind:"defer_due",result:<receipt>}`. First201/replay200, no-store. Изменённое тело
под исходным key конфликтует; journal failure откатывает due update.

102 additive migration добавляет три узких индекса и command kind defer_due,
сохраняя099–101 и прежние immutable/Namespace guards. SQL/PG source tests покрывают
fairness/backoff, rollback, exact revision/time key, concurrent reserve, held
revocation, admit advancement и admitted-disable continuity. Real HTTP source
покрывает due limit/auth и original defer replay. Это ещё не compiled/qualified
candidate; Fleet manual-priority journal/runtime wiring и общие gates отдельно.

### Original reserve recovery after revoke: next source candidate

Only the exact original configured Fleet machine may read its retained Reserve/Admit
operation after human owner revocation. Project, machine, immutable execution,
grant/fence and full retained binding must match; another actor/project cannot
read it. The response is the historical receipt, including historical fields,
not a fresh dispatch grant. Fresh grant, admission and new reservation still
require current owner authority. This API-only correction needs no DDL, is not
part of frozen102/4fe, and awaits its own PG/HTTP qualification. READ-only Fleet
credentials retain their prior original-read behavior only with fresh active-owner
project READ; protective recovery after revocation requires original READ+WRITE.

### Перепроверка исходного сценария: следующий кандидат в исходниках

`BugSearchSnapshot.verification_basis` — optional отчёт finding с подтверждённым
producer: typed source/source_identity, title, basis, expected, actual, reproducer,
checked_version и evidence_refs. None опускается; хеши прежних Search snapshot и
чтение истории не меняются. Новый reserve перепроверки требует этот basis,
ручной QA-режим, UUID реального Bug, одну выбранную доставленную цель и её
`expected_fixed_deployment_ref`.

Цель должна точно входить в принятую policy проекта: repository_ref, target_ref
и canonical source branch. Scope, exclusions, revision и owner сохраняются.
Поэтому Bug можно перепроверить в проекте с несколькими репозиториями, не
подставляя один delivery ID разным приложениям. Обычный Search по-прежнему
требует полный упорядоченный набор policy targets. Репозиторий исходного basis
должен совпадать с выбранной целью; исправленный commit может отличаться от
первоначально проверенного.

Перед reserve Tracker сверяет basis с существующим Bug, immutable source,
завершённым creation receipt и сохранённым occurrence. Новые grant/admit также
проверяют доступность этой связи. Сетевых запросов под SQL-блокировками нет.
Отсутствующий, удалённый, перемещённый или чужой Bug не даёт разрешения на запуск.
Восстановление исходного protective receipt не меняется. Purpose, UUID Bug и
ожидаемая доставка сохраняются в существующих execution columns; DDL не нужен.

Завершённый технический результат Workflow содержит строгий `verification`:
`{bug_id,basis_sha256,delivery_ref,verdict,actual,evidence_refs}`. Хеш basis
охватывает полный исходный типизированный отчёт; Bug и доставка совпадают со
snapshot. Verdict — passed|failed|inconclusive. Passed/failed требуют полного
покрытия и подтверждённых before/after `qa_same_version` observations. Оба
наблюдения должны совпадать с выбранными configuration/repository UUID, project,
target, delivery, commit и неизменной serving identity. Частичное покрытие
допускает только inconclusive. Выход native процесса и пустые findings не
означают, что Bug исправлен.

Регрессии в исходниках проверяют прежние wire/hash, новый commit в том же
репозитории, чужие repositories/configurations, несовпадения basis/verdict,
policy membership, реальную registration→reserve→admit→grant и восстановление
исходного receipt после отзыва доступа. Добавлен настоящий HTTP-сценарий Tracker;
его runtime/CI carriers явно synthetic. Квалификация ещё не завершена;
capabilities, автопоиск и бизнес-переходы кандидатом не включаются. Результаты
конкретных неизменных прогонов фиксируются в delivery evidence Fleet.


Следующий source-кандидат original Tracker100 поддерживает дополнительную closed
custody `unprepared_successor_cancelled`. Она требует actual context UUID и
bounded exact SDK carrier с command/origin/predecessor/family manifest/native
creation request/execution source hashes. `state=cancelled`, наблюдение строго
`unprepared_successor_cancelled`; runtime exit/container/run refs не выдумываются.
Это положительный Base creation/family no-create CAS под exact Fleet producer
attestation, не вывод из отсутствующего journal или локального attempt counter.
Используются прежние cancel endpoint, immutable original key/body/receipt,
protective readback после owner revoke и contradiction guards; новый DDL не
нужен. Tracker101 не принимает эту custody. Старые null/None bytes не меняются.
Domain+PG regression source написаны, compile/PG UNRUN; actual Base/Fleet source
adoption и native qualification остаются отдельными gates.
